l":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Swamp","oracle_id":"56719f6a-1a6c-4c0a-8d21-18f7d7350b68","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {B}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["B"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land \u2014 Swamp"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Morbid"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{B}","name":"Tragic Slip","oracle_id":"fa6e2a47-a8cb-4224-ae3e-f61c90477285","oracle_text":"Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.\nMorbid \u2014 That creature gets -13/-13 until end of turn instead if a creature died this turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-01-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Defender"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{W}","name":"Wall of Omens","oracle_id":"5f601f48-d24b-4883-9fde-b3f620e7c9ea","oracle_text":"Defender\nWhen this creature enters, draw a card.","power":"0","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2025-04-11","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Wall"}],"rulings":[{"comment":"If Rest in Peace is destroyed by a spell, Rest in Peace will be exiled and then the spell will be put into its owner's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card is discarded while Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that function when a card is discarded (such as madness) still work, even though that card never reaches a graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of a discarded card (such as Chandra Ablaze's first ability) can find that card in exile.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While Rest in Peace is on the battlefield, abilities that trigger whenever a creature dies won't trigger because cards and tokens are never put into a player's graveyard.","oracle_id":"087f9ad7-e74f-40e2-8102-1ed2925d0418","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Changeling applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Crib Swap tries to resolve, the spell won't resolve. No player will create a Shapeshifter token.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Kindred is a card type (like creature or instant), not a supertype (like legendary).","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Kindred is a card type that allows noncreature cards to have creature types. For example, Echoes of Eternity is an Eldrazi (although not a creature) while on the battlefield and an Eldrazi card (although not a creature card) in zones other than the battlefield.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This card was originally printed with the \"tribal\" card type. That card type has been replaced with \"kindred\". This change does not affect the gameplay function of this card.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Changeling is a characteristic-defining ability. It functions in all zones, not only while a card that has it is on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes a creature with changeling to become a new creature type, it will be only that new creature type (unless the effect says \"in addition\" or similar). It will still have changeling; the effect making it all creature types will simply be overwritten.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes a creature with changeling to lose all abilities, it will remain all creature types, even though it will no longer have changeling. This is because changeling applies before the effect that removes it.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Kindred is a card type that allows noncreature cards to have creature types. For example, Morcant's Eyes is an Elf (although not a creature) while on the battlefield and an Elf card (although not a creature card) in zones other than the battlefield.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some older cards were originally printed with the \"tribal\" card type. That card type has been replaced with \"kindred.\" This change does not affect the gameplay function of these cards.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The subtype Shapeshifter that appears on the type line is mostly there to reinforce the flavor. A creature card with changeling is just as much a Kithkin, a Goblin, a Merfolk, and a Brushwagg as it is a Shapeshifter.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While it appears only on cards that already have other card types, kindred is a card type and will be counted by effects that refer to the number of card types among cards in a zone.","oracle_id":"2987c385-011a-4032-a516-a46d1e9dc9e8","published_at":"2025-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You target the creature that will be sacrificed when you cast Mercy Killing, then its controller (who may or may not be you) sacrifices it when Mercy Killing resolves. Because this is a sacrifice, neither regeneration nor indestructible will save the creature.","oracle_id":"4d80bac5-ce62-4c5c-873a-ce81d2697842","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target permanent is an illegal target by the time Beast Within tries to resolve, the spell won't resolve. No player creates a Beast token. If the target is legal but not destroyed (most likely because it has indestructible), its controller does create a Beast token.","oracle_id":"7735eeba-693b-47e2-bd51-414379cf1016","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
